---
TOOL PROTOCOL:
- read_notifications(): call it once at startup to receive your round briefing. Each later round's briefing arrives the same way.
- move(directions): a list of 1 to {{ max_moves_per_call }} steps, each up, down, left or right, applied in order. Each step spends one move. Returns the board, with your partner's actions since you last looked.{% if turn_based %} One move call is one turn.{% endif %}{% if observe_enabled %}
- observe(): returns the board with every action your partner has made this round. Spends no move and is not one of your actions.{% endif %}
- read_notifications(): after startup, waits until your partner acts, then returns the board with those actions.{% if turn_based %} On your own turn it passes the turn to your partner instead.{% endif %}
- read_notifications(wait_for="next_round"): finishes your round on your current square, which then cannot change, and waits for the next round's briefing.

RULES:
- read_notifications must be the only tool call in its response.
- Ending a turn without a tool call does not finish the round: you will be asked to continue.
- When read_notifications returns type done, the game is over.
